What was ported
---------------
The claim-extraction prompt (LONG_FORM_ANSWER_PROMPT) and the entailment
prompt (NLI_STATEMENTS_MESSAGE) from ragas v0.1.21 were copied VERBATIM
into internal/eval/faithfulness.go as Go string constants. The two
prompts drive the Faithfulness metric's two-stage algorithm:

  1. ExtractClaims(answer) -> atomic, pronoun-free claims
  2. Entails(claim, retrievedContext) -> per-claim verdict (1/0)

Faithfulness = (supported claims) / (total claims).

Why port verbatim
-----------------
The point is the exact "Ragas 口径" (industry-comparable headline number).
Ragas's calibration-sensitive engineering is concentrated in claim
extraction (handles negation, modality, temporal claims, multi-sentence
answers). Paraphrasing the prompt would silently drift the score away
from the industry-standard Ragas number, defeating the purpose of using
the Ragas name as the validation reference. The ported text is left
UNMODIFIED so attribution is unambiguous and downstream reviewers can
diff against the canonical source.

The other 3 metrics in internal/eval (answer_relevancy,
context_precision, context_recall) use simple Go-authored yes/no judge
prompts — they are NOT derived from Ragas and carry no Ragas attribution.

